window.DECISIONS={"clarifications": ["Quick actions", "Q1 Scope and ownership — Business clarification required. Who may create/edit/delete projects, plans, masters and batches? Which admin roles can approve, upload, close registration or grant access? Define ERNET, state and school boundaries, trainer assignment limits, and student versus teacher rights. [; A1–A6; 1–11]", "Q2 Project source and values — Business clarification required. What Odoo data is provided? What are “values”? Is project code entered, supplied by Odoo or automatically populated? Are duplicate projects prohibited? What happens if Odoo is unavailable? [1.1; both 1.2]", "Q3 Fields and dates — Business clarification required. Which fields are mandatory beyond the explicitly optional descriptions? What are length limits, permitted characters, date order, project/batch date boundaries, past-date limits and any time cutoff? None is stated here. [1–3]", "Q4 Availability and holidays — Business clarification required. Can availability be changed for today or earlier? What constitutes availability, including hours and overlapping batches? Which state applies, who maintains holidays and does a holiday/conflict block scheduling or permit override? [A3; A5; 3.4]", "Q5 Training plans — Reusable masters, minimum four days, stable unique codes and batch snapshot history are confirmed by the revised v4.8 requirements. Production approval authority and concurrent editing remain to be defined.", "Q6 Master resources and certification — Business clarification required. Who creates and approves forms, trainer records and templates? How are resources assigned to days? Does access end when project dates change? How are certificates issued, and under what completion/attendance conditions? [A1–A4]", "Q7 Upload contract — Business clarification required. For batch, trainee and multimedia uploads, define allowed extensions including XLS/XLSX and video types, sizes, exact column headings/order, mandatory values, formats and reference checks. Define error review, duplicates, failed rows, all-or-nothing versus partial saving, retries, saved-record visibility and confirmation. [A6; 3; 4; second 10.2]", "Q8 Batch identity and capacity — Business clarification required. Is Batch_UniqueID unique globally or by project? How is it supplied? What values are allowed for Batch_Maxsize? How does capacity apply per location? Can capacity be reduced below current enrolment? [3.2; 4]", "Q9 Registration window — Business clarification required. Confirm Day 1 only or alternative logic expressly left to business. Define opening/closing time, timezone, effect of closing registration, and whether subsequent Excel upload remains permitted after final batch closure. [3.2 note; 4.2–4.3]", "Q10 Trainee approval — Business clarification required. Which trainer approves? Can entries be rejected or edited? What counts as a junk registration? Must the entire list be approved? Define duplicate trainee identity, re-registration, batch closure and reopened-batch rules. [4.4]", "Q11 Student and attendance scope — The 5 October 2026 user update confirms attendance bulk upload, authorized modification, audit and trainee/batch/date linkage. Student assignment, exact additional-role grants, batch-date exceptions, final-closure corrections and any correction cutoff/approval still require business clarification.", "Q12 Resource visibility — Business clarification required. Define common versus project-specific eligibility, access rights and approved upload process. Confirm older-batch access on subsequent edits/removals, plan versions and completed-project access. The source note says newly added “requires”; it is read in resource context, but wording should be confirmed. [A6; 5 note]", "Q13 Dashboard and MIS definitions — Business clarification required. Define each role dashboard, metrics, filters and refresh timing; define completion, performance, user lifecycle and resource-access measurements. Confirm Excel download rights, audit details and retention. [7–8]", "Q14 Personal information — Business clarification required. Business must define captured personal fields. Reconcile partial report masking, database masked storage/display, clear name only on final certificate and encryption of all database data. Explain how clear certificate names are retrieved and how names/email/mobile are handled elsewhere. [8.2; 10.3–10.4; Notes]", "Q15 Login and OTP — Business clarification required. Does “Multiple file login attempts” mean failed attempts? What count triggers 15 minutes, what scope and reset logic apply? Define OTP expiry minutes, delivery, retries, lookup matches and failure messages. [9; 10.1; 10.5]", "Q16 URL and security implementation — Business clarification required. What does hiding a clear URL mean for users? Define required input checks, extension allowlists, transport/storage controls and permitted administrative actions. Source numbering repeats 10.2; both rules are retained. [10–11]", "Q17 Project administrator exception — Business clarification required. How should two-project administrators switch projects, and what if more than two are linked? Does automatic selection also apply to other project-specific users? [Notes]", "Q18 Action failure responses — Business clarification required. Approve messages and behavior for failed create/save/edit/delete/upload/submit/approval actions, unauthorized access and unavailable dependencies; the source supplies no exact wording. [1–11]", "Trainee Registration update — Business clarification required: final date window; email applicability/mobile mandatory status; OTP delivery, expiry, retry and disclosure policy; duplicate identity scope; Admin grants; post-closure changes.", "Training / Learning Resources update — Business clarification required: approval authority and linking roles; exact multimedia formats/size/MIME checks; completed-batch propagation and reversal; timing/day restriction for materials; trainer grant scope and expiry.", "Training Plan update — Business clarification required: exact edit/approval roles; description required and length limits; code format/global scope; duration/calendar rules; historical-change approval/version activation/deletion/rollback; revised plan code policy and completed-batch resource additions.", "Batch / Trainee v3.4 — Business clarification required: exact Admin batch grants and deletion/reopening/retention policy; workbook XLS/columns/sizes/partial save; ID scope/format, field limits; live UDISE/availability/holiday integration; registration final date/contact/OTP/duplicates policy."], "assumptions": ["A01: Baseline attachment requirements are retained together with later explicit user updates. Later confirmed requirements include attendance bulk upload, master data, role login, resources, certificates and provided Schoolnet branding; earlier unconfirmed field limits remain unresolved.", "A02: Demo scopes: central all; ERNET project P1; state P1+Karnataka; school P1+school S1; trainer T1 assigned batches; trainee U1 self. Monitoring admins read only. Schoolnet writes projects/plans/batches/masters/users/templates. Trainer approves own batch, marks attendance and bulk registers. Detailed grants require Q1.", "A03: Demo scaffold fields necessary to create meaningful records are marked required, but undocumented mandatory status is flagged. Descriptions optional. No character caps or forbidden-character patterns invented; text safely escaped.", "A04: Plan days and capacity are positive integers; day numbering starts at 1; batch end >= start. Generated UUID-derived codes globally unique. Planned trainee counts use capacity, not confirmed targets.", "A05: Availability means a single interval covers entire batch; holidays block, no override. No invented overlapping-batch/hour restriction. Actual school location from synthetic UDISE directory. Batch dates within project enforced despite Q3 conflict.", "A06: Excel demo uses XLSX first worksheet, named headers, all-or-nothing save with row errors. XLS binary unsupported (explicit error). File size has no business cap; browser memory/quota may fail. Capacity, reference and duplicates validated across staged rows.", "A07: Duplicate trainee key mobile OR email within a batch. All synthetic identities masked on tables/downloads. Demo stores original synthetic names unencrypted; does not satisfy production masking/encryption.", "A08: Demo self-registration default Day 1 only in Asia/Kolkata, configurable review option. Fixed displayed OTP 123456 is simulation, no delivery/expiry/rate limit. No actual authentication; persona selector is not security.", "A09: Manual attendance saves a complete trainee list with explicit Present/Absent. Bulk XLSX supports selected-batch rows, adds or corrects marks and leaves missing rows unchanged. No future dates; no invented previous-date cutoff. Batch-period bounds, duplicate workbook rejection, atomic save and blocking final-closure corrections are documented POC contracts.", "A10: Used plan structural changes locked; metadata changes audited. Batch deletion with children blocked. Started batch dates locked until policy defined. Final closure blocks subsequent imports, requires approved list and configured completion evidence; no reopening/cancellation/drop action fabricated.", "A11: Conditional new-resource propagation defaults off for used plans. Common resource creation admin-only demo; trainer upload needs reviewer explicit grant. Bytes retained in IndexedDB, metadata in localStorage; sample resource available as local text document.", "A12: Completion/certification thresholds start unset. Review settings may temporarily specify attendance, assessment pass and form requirements, visibly provisional. Demo certificates are previews, require configured criteria, assigned trainer approval and evidence; no production issuance.", "A13: KPI formulas and report fields documented below; recommended views supported with browser evidence only. Missing authoritative targets, scores/history/login data are shown pending/N/A, not fabricated. Alerts without defined thresholds shown as decisions pending.", "A15: Training days map to consecutive calendar dates from batch start for this review. Excluding holidays/weekends, daily duration, plan duration versus batch date span, and plan-day completion semantics require Q4/Q5 confirmation. Exact-answer scoring is a temporary demonstration method; no real assessment rubric is supplied.", "A14: No project/plan/resource delete control when document does not define deletion policy; central project date modification revalidates dependent batches. Demo Excel/CSV export; PDF via print/save-as-PDF. Local download rights conservative central/monitoring roles; trainee self and trainer assigned evidence only.", "A16: Trainee Registration user update: batch links allow new unassigned entrants. OTP requests bind to batch, purpose and normalized contacts only in memory; fixed displayed 123456 remains simulated without delivery/expiry. Mobile OR email accepted provisionally; final applicability/mandatory policy requires business clarification. Lookup available after registration closes; final closure still blocks new imports.", "A17: v3.2 resource update supersedes A11 resource linking/propagation details. Upload requires project+plan. Individual trainer grants override default grant. Trainer requests common reuse; Admin publication is provisional. Per-link include-existing flag defaults off; baseline links retain legacy setting. Materials immediately available once link applies until project expiry; form day gates retained. MP4/WEBM are demo video defaults with explicit admin review extension list; file bytes use IndexedDB, metadata/links/grants use localStorage.", "A19: v3.4 Schoolnet controls individual scoped ERNET/State/School Admin batchManage grants. Trainee-management granted to scoped managers and assigned trainers; approval remains assigned trainer only. Batch Excel preview and commit plus manual editing use same rules. Location is derived from sample UDISE directory; reference text remains separate. Linked/closed records protected. All v3.1 trainee assumptions remain open and labelled.", "A18: v4.8 supersedes project-owned plans and used-plan locks. Reusable masters require a minimum four-day whole-number duration; batches use immutable assigned snapshots. Master modifications apply to future assignments. Explicit resource propagation is audited and constrained to project scope and snapshot duration. Codes are unique per local demo database; server-wide concurrency is outside this POC."], "ux": ["Searchable project and plan choices via labelled search + native select (keyboard-friendly).", "Review invalid Excel rows before any save; download templates; preserve input after failed validation.", "Project context in shared topbar, automatic sole-project selection; responsive ivory navigation.", "Evidence-based completion panel, decision register and rules available inside prototype.", "Local reset with confirmation, clear loading/error/empty states and audit links."], "screens": [["dashboard", "§13–17,27", "Review scoped progress", "All", "Data in permitted scope", "Choose persona → context → KPIs → drill into records"], ["projects", "§3,5", "Create/manage project", "Schoolnet Admin (demo)", "Sample Odoo project", "Search Odoo → choose → dates → validate → save"], ["plans", "§4.5,6", "Define plan and day activities", "Schoolnet Admin (demo)", "Independent resource/form repository", "Create reusable master → configure multiple resources per day → staged save → assign to batch"], ["batches", "§7", "Schedule groups", "Schoolnet Admin (demo)", "Project, plan, school, trainer availability/holidays", "Excel select → parse → row preview → validate → commit; manual create/edit fallback"], ["trainees", "§8", "Bulk register/approve/close", "Assigned Trainer/Admin", "Batch and capacity", "Select batch → import list → trainer approves each → close registration → final closure evaluation"], ["registration", "§8", "Self-register / ID lookup", "Trainee", "Open batch, review window, demo OTP", "Open batch link → enter synthetic contacts → demo OTP → register / lookup"], ["resources", "§4.4,9", "Upload/link/access content", "Admin/permitted trainer/trainee viewer", "Project + plan + permission + day gate", "Select bytes → format validation → IndexedDB storage → link day → access"], ["attendance", "§10", "Record daily attendance", "Assigned Trainer/Admin demo", "Batch and trainees, date <= today", "Select project → batch → training day/date → view/mark trainees or Excel preview → validated save with audit"], ["assessments", "§4.5,11,17", "Complete linked assessments/feedback", "Trainee; Admin form master", "Linked day available", "Create demo form master → plan/day link → trainee enters answer → submit evidence"], ["completion", "§11,29", "Evaluate closure and learner evidence", "Admin/assigned Trainer", "Approval, days/attendance/forms, review config", "Open batch → inspect evidence → evaluate → close only if all eligible"], ["certificates", "§12,29", "Configure template and preview", "Admin demo; trainee own preview", "Configured eligibility and completion evidence", "Configure fields/logos/colors → evaluate learner → download marked demo preview"], ["masters", "§4", "Manage pool/availability/holiday/form", "Admin; trainer own availability", "Central masters", "Add trainer/interval/holiday/form → edit/remove availability → assignments view"], ["users", "§2,23–24", "Role assignments and profile", "Admin; own profile", "Synthetic users", "Create/edit grants → project scope → masked profile audit"], ["reports", "§18–26", "Inspect/export nine MIS views", "Scoped authorized viewer", "Scoped records, common filters", "Select report → filter → table → actual XLSX/CSV or print"], ["audit", "§10,24,28", "Inspect important changes", "Scoped authorized viewer", "Recorded mutations", "Filter masked events → inspect before/after"], ["review", "§29,Q1–Q18", "Resolve review decisions", "Review facilitator", "Catalogue/clarifications/assumptions", "Inspect source → rules/traceability → temporary settings → review impact"]]};
